    "body": "Stopped at Step 7 of the assigned worker instructions.\n\nThe quick gate failed only in sodick_alc400g::a_tapered_punch_is_refused_at_post_while_the_file_states_no_guide_heights.\nGeneration rejects missing edm.lower_guide_z and edm.upper_guide_z before that test reaches posting.\nThe targeted gate failed the same way on unchanged commit 62e1d36a655a71407ff7a9980057db3c8cc8197a.\nThat commit was upstream/main when this worktree was created.\nI restored all four changed production files for the baseline check, and git diff --exit-code HEAD confirmed no tracked differences.\nPR #1857 corrected this existing test in commit 0e1f3709 while the gate was running.\nI did not merge that unrelated change.\n\nThe local #1499 fix adds optional edm.sodick_tank and edm.sodick_flushing settings.\nI chose machine settings because the existing edit_machine MCP tool already applies them through undoable commands.\nI dropped separate operation fields because the issue permits machine settings and those fields would expand the change.\nThe Sodick post emits the requested tank word before threading and the flushing word afterward.\nUnstated settings preserve the existing golden.\nSeven post pins and two app pins pass with the fix.\nBaseline rollback and nine individual validation mutations all fail their pins, then pass after restoration.\nClippy passes for camcraft-post and camcraft-app with all targets and warnings denied.\nOne new golden differs from the existing golden only in its header and the T94/T84 insertions.\n\nThe claim is released under the instruction to stop after two real gate failures.\nThe fixed sources are restored locally on issue/1499-sodick-flushing in .claude/worktrees/issue-1499 of the CamcraftPool checkout.\nThe patch is uncommitted and unpushed.\nNo PR was opened.\nFailure and mutation logs remain outside the branch in /tmp/1499-*.log.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
